Name the OpenHarmony version in a phone's User-Agent.

A phone sends Chrome's reduced Android User-Agent. Put the OpenHarmony
version in front of the Android token, "Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; OpenHarmony
7.0; Android 10; K) ...", so that sites looking for HarmonyOS find it
while everything else still reads an Android phone. The version is the
system's (OH_GetOSFullName), major.minor, as the tablet and PC strings
already carry it; the client hints stay Android. Tablets and PCs are
unchanged.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-phone-ua-openharmony.patch

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -294,8 +294,16 @@ std::string BuildOhosUserAgent(const std::string& product, bool mobile) {
   // to bot checks (Cloudflare Turnstile failed with 600010). The platform,
   // platform version, navigator.platform and navigator.plugins all follow
   // this string; see GetPlatformForUAMetadata() below.
-  return base::StrCat({"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 10; K) AppleWebKit/537.36 "
-                       "(KHTML, like Gecko) ",
+  //
+  // With the OpenHarmony version in front of the Android token, as in
+  // "Linux; OpenHarmony 7.0; Android 10; K": sites that look for HarmonyOS
+  // find it, and everything else still reads an Android phone. The client
+  // hints stay Android, so the string and navigator.userAgentData agree.
+  return base::StrCat({"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; ",
+                       major_minor.empty()
+                           ? std::string()
+                           : base::StrCat({"OpenHarmony ", major_minor, "; "}),
+                       "Android 10; K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) ",
                        product, " Mobile Safari/537.36"});
 }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
